# libxkbfile -- the XKB file and .xkm reader, shared by the X server and by
# xkbcomp.
#
# It is the format library sitting between the two halves of the keymap path:
# xkbcomp compiles xkeyboard-config's rules into a binary .xkm using it, and
# Xwayland reads that .xkm back with the same code. Xwayland takes it as
# `dependency('xkbfile')` with no `required: false` and no option guarding it
# (meson.build:104), so unlike most of that file this one fails loudly.
#
# NOT THE SAME THING AS libxkbcommon, which this tree already has. libxkbcommon
# is the client-side and compositor-side keymap library -- mutter compiles a
# keymap with it and hands the result to Wayland clients. libxkbfile is the
# X11-side one, and the X server's own keymap path does not go through
# libxkbcommon at all: it shells out to xkbcomp. Both are needed, for different
# halves of the same session.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://www.x.org/pub/individual/lib/libxkbfile-1.1.3.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=a9b63eea997abb9ee6a8b4fbb515831c841f471af845a09de443b28003874bec
SRC_DIR=libxkbfile-1.1.3

# THE TARBALL SHIPS BOTH A configure AND A meson.build, AND THIS RECIPE USES
# AUTOTOOLS. Not indifference: the two are not equivalent here. The autotools
# build is the one upstream generates the release from -- it is what produced
# the configure in the tarball -- and it is what every other X library in this
# tree is built with, so the flags and the resulting layout match its
# neighbours rather than being a one-off.
#
# --disable-static is the only flag: configure.ac 43-52 has no feature options
# at all, just AC_CHECK_FUNCS probes and one PKG_CHECK_MODULES for x11 and
# kbproto. There is nothing here to pin.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static"
